    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2VYqMS7K4Fjg3scyUvmRDty)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main` (at `b09d4e0`); docs only, no code and no tangled block changed, no CHANGELOG edit.\n- Conflicts with #419 (open): it rewrites the top of `sp-devonthink.org` and moves the DEVONthink docs to `docs/tangles/devonthink/`.\n  - Merge this one first, or keep my \"Current state\" section and the new `Overview` bullets when resolving.\n  - The section's relative links (`file:sp-reading.org` etc.) work in `docs/tangles/academic/`; after #419's move the links to non-DEVONthink docs need `../academic/`.\n- After merging: nothing to retarget.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `sp-devonthink.org`: new section **Current state**, as bullets and tables:\n  - what exists and which PR delivered it (#414, #415, #418, #441, #454 and follow-ups, #460, #449, #444);\n  - what each module does, in a few bullets;\n  - all keys under the unified leader (`C-; k d …`, `C-; B a`, `C-; k l`, `C-; E`), the Embark record actions, and the removal of `C-c k d` (#484, #489);\n  - options per module, including `sp-fetch-inbox-profile` and the `DT_OPEN_*` settings (`DT_OPEN_RAISE` = `window`, `app` or `none`);\n  - the Hammerspoon highlight keys of `b09d4e0` (no PR);\n  - open PRs not on `main` (#419, #420, #421, #451, #443, #455) and the closed #452, which is not described as a feature;\n  - known limitations and what is untested.\n- Top of `sp-devonthink.org`: status line and intro updated; the link to the older `devonthink-emacs-integration.org` is kept, plus a link to it at `c0188a9f`.\n- `sp-devonthink-{browse,tags,search,bibsync}.org`: one bullet pointing to \"Current state\"; bibsync now says #455 is not on `main`.\n- `README.org`: `sp-devonthink` row extended, and a short DEVONthink bullet list under the `academic/` table.\n\n## Not done or not checked\n\n- No Emacs in the container: `tools/check-tangle.sh` could not run. No `emacs-lisp` block was edited, so the tangled `.el` files should still match.\n- The module code and PR texts were read, not run; \"untested\" lists repeat what the module docs and PR bodies say, not Sia's manual test results.\n- The Hammerspoon file's header comment says `Cmd+Option+Space`; the code binds `Cmd+Ctrl+Alt+H`. The doc follows the code.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Open `sp-devonthink.org`, section \"Current state\": follow the links to the module docs, `devonthink-open/README.org` and the c0188a9f link.\n- [ ] In `README.org`, follow the \"Current state\" link under the `academic/` table.\n- [ ] `bash tools/check-tangle.sh` still says all modules match their docs.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiB8aYxfMBuTwtyuJV6)_",
